## Description Custom Azure model configuration sends unsupported temperature value. The issue appears to be caused by a default or internally overridden temperature value being sent instead of the value defined in `modelOptions`.  When using the following custom Azure model configuration in VS Code Copilot:  ```json {   "name": "Azure",   "vendor": "azure",   "apiKey": "${input:chat.lm.secret.xyz}",   "models": [     {       "id": "gpt-5.6-luna",       "name": "GPT 5.6 Luna",       "url": "https://example.com/api/dev/chat/completions",       "toolCalling": true,       "vision": true,       "maxInputTokens": 128000,       "maxOutputTokens": 16000,       "modelOptions": {         "temperature": 1       }     }   ] } ```  the request fails with HTTP `400`.  The configured temperature is `1`, which is the only value supported by this model. However, the error indicates that VS Code Copilot sends `temperature: 0.1` in the request.  ## Error message  ```text Sorry, your request failed. Please try again.  Client Request Id: 74171b3c-cee2-44bd-b121-b258a1058507  Reason: Request Failed: 400 {"detail":"{
  "error": {
    "message": "Unsupported value: 'temperature' does not support 0.1 with this model. Only the default (1) value is supported.",
    "type": "invalid_request_error",
    "param": "temperature",
    "code": "unsupported_value"
  }
}"} ```  ## Expected behavior  VS Code Copilot should either:  1. Respect the configured value:     ```json    "modelOptions": {      "temperature": 1    }    ```  2. Omit the `temperature` parameter when the model only supports its default value.  ## Actual behavior  The request contains:  ```json "temperature": 0.1 ```  despite the configuration specifying:  ```json "temperature": 1 ```  As a result, the Azure endpoint rejects the request with HTTP `400`.  ## Environment  - VS Code: `1.137.` - GitHub Copilot Chat extension: `0.41 (2026-03-25)` - Provider: Azure-compatible endpoint - Model: `gpt-5.6-luna` - Endpoint: `https://example.com/api/dev/chat/completions`  ## Additional information  I created proxy server which capture API request, update temperature value, and sends modified request with proper temperature value directly to a model to make copilot work properly.
